---
title: "Installation"
description: "Install qql-go on macOS, Linux, or Windows using the install script, PowerShell, go install, or from source."
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

## macOS / Linux

{% terminal title="Install script" %}
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/srimon12/qql-go/main/install.sh | sh
{% /terminal %}

## Windows (PowerShell)

{% terminal title="PowerShell" %}
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/srimon12/qql-go/main/install.ps1 | iex
{% /terminal %}

## Go Install

{% terminal title="go install" %}
go install github.com/srimon12/qql-go/cmd/qql-go@latest
{% /terminal %}

## From Source

{% terminal title="Build from source" %}
git clone https://github.com/srimon12/qql-go.git
cd qql-go
go build -o qql-go ./cmd/qql-go
{% /terminal %}

## Verify Installation

{% terminal title="Verify" %}
qql-go version
qql-go doctor
{% /terminal %}

---

## Binary Name

| Platform | Binary name |
|---|---|
| macOS / Linux | `qql-go` |
| Windows | `qql-go.exe` |

---

## PATH Setup

The install script puts the binary on your PATH automatically. If you installed somewhere custom, set the `QQL_BIN` environment variable to the absolute path. The CLI checks: `QQL_BIN` env var → `qql-go` on `$PATH` → repo-local fallback.

{% terminal title="macOS / Linux" %}
export QQL_BIN=/absolute/path/to/qql-go
{% /terminal %}

{% terminal title="Windows (PowerShell)" %}
$env:QQL_BIN = "C:\path\to\qql-go.exe"
{% /terminal %}

---

## Prerequisites

| Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|
| **Go 1.24+** | Only needed if building from source or using `go install` |
| **Qdrant instance** | Docker, native, or Qdrant Cloud |
| **Embedding server** | Only needed for `--inference-mode local` or `external` |

### Start Qdrant with Docker

{% terminal title="Docker" %}
docker run -p 6333:6333 -p 6334:6334 qdrant/qdrant
{% /terminal %}

{% aside type="note" title="Port 6334" %}

QQL connects to Qdrant on port **6334** (gRPC). Port 6333 (REST) is used by the HTTP API but not by QQL directly. Passing port 6333 will be rejected with an error.

{% /aside %}

